 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532688,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You are making a casserole that includes vegetable soup and pasta. The size of your cylindrical casserole dish has a diameter of 10 inches and is 4 inches high. The pasta will consume the bottom portion of the casserole dish about 1 inch high. The soup can has a diameter of 3 inches and is 4 inches high. After the pasta is added, how many cans of soup can you add?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The volume of a right cylinder with radius <i>r</i> and height <i>h</i> is <span data-math=\"V = \\pi {r^2}h\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Find the volume of the casserole dish available.</p>\n<p>The depth of the dish is 4 inches, but one inch is filled with pasta. Use 3 inches for the height of the cylinder. The diameter is 10 inches, so the radius is 5 inches.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"V = \\pi {r^2}h = \\pi {\\left( {{\\text{5 in}}} \\right)^2}\\left( {{\\text{3 in}}} \\right) = 75\\pi {\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^3}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Find the volume of a can. The diameter is 3 inches, so the radius is 1.5 inches.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"V = \\pi {r^2}h = \\pi {\\left( {{\\text{1}}{\\text{.5 in}}} \\right)^2}\\left( {{\\text{4 in}}} \\right) = 9\\pi {\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^3}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 3: Make a conversion factor using the volume of a can.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"75\\pi \\cancel{{{\\text{ inche}}{{\\text{s}}^3}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1{\\text{ can}}}}{{9\\pi {\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{inche}}{{\\text{s}}^3}}}}}} \\right) = \\frac{{25}}{3}{\\text{ cans}} = 8\\frac{1}{3}{\\text{ cans}}\"></span></p>\n<p>You can add <span data-math=\"8\\frac{1}{3}\"></span> cans of soup.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "approximately 8 1/3 cans of soup"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
